{"parentUuid": "712cbb30-5bbe-491c-bbc0-a5bf8115db16", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5", "id": "msg_01Cu7uNELBeWYYGSbLBPB4UR", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_011HrwrsyOcBXSXMcaJz6r2L", "name": "Agent", "input": {"description": "Map canvas render/culling path", "prompt": "In /Users/divadbaroon/Desktop/engelbart-canvas, map how the canvas decides which cards to draw each frame: which file computes visibility, what the viewport object looks like (fields, units: screen px vs world units), and where zoom/pan are applied. Quote the relevant functions. Read-only.", "subagent_type": "Explore"}}], "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1174, "cache_read_input_tokens": 20420, "output_tokens": 117, "service_tier": "standard"}}, "requestId": "req_011CxYB5SWmx45Jb9PbpuZbv", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "0c2d8bb7-1193-4c70-a918-d6106be8eccc", "timestamp": "2026-09-02T05:41:08.201Z", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "cli", "cwd": "/Users/divadbaroon/Desktop/engelbart-canvas", "sessionId": "a2f80be0-c548-4c0f-add0-bdf6bd4a276f", "version": "2.1.246", "gitBranch": "fix/canvas-zoom-cull"}
{"parentUuid": "0c2d8bb7-1193-4c70-a918-d6106be8eccc", "isSidechain": false, "promptId": "72ec86d0-ca08-40c3-818e-f51e4f1014df", "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_011HrwrsyOcBXSXMcaJz6r2L", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Visibility is computed in `src/renderer/canvas/culling.js` `visibleCards(cards, vp, margin=120)`. The viewport (`viewport.js` `makeViewport`) has width/height/panX/panY in **screen px** and `zoom`; the camera maps `screen = world * zoom + pan`, and `toWorld` divides by zoom. `visibleCards` compares card world coordinates against `-panX .. -panX + width` without dividing by zoom, i.e. it mixes screen px with world units. Called once per frame from `CanvasView.jsx` (`const shown = visibleCards(cards, vp)`)."}]}]}, "uuid": "bf224228-1bb9-48bc-a689-d79f6dbc0a4e", "timestamp": "2026-09-02T05:41:45.861Z", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "cli", "cwd": "/Users/divadbaroon/Desktop/engelbart-canvas", "sessionId": "a2f80be0-c548-4c0f-add0-bdf6bd4a276f", "version": "2.1.246", "gitBranch": "fix/canvas-zoom-cull"}
{"parentUuid": "bf224228-1bb9-48bc-a689-d79f6dbc0a4e", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5", "id": "msg_01VAYKVroEIAZv00KJe7RINQ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "That's the bug: `visibleCards` builds the visible rectangle in screen pixels but compares it to card positions in world units. At zoom 1 they coincide; at zoom 0.35 the real visible world area is ~2.9× wider and taller than what the function checks, so everything right of/below that box is culled. I'll compute the rectangle through `toWorld` so it's correct at any zoom, and scale the margin too."}], "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2544, "cache_read_input_tokens": 32520, "output_tokens": 107, "service_tier": "standard"}}, "requestId": "req_011CMN32KMEQSt9fmcrdHUyR", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "1d89add3-a91f-4ce7-bd9b-70873a98c498", "timestamp": "2026-09-02T05:41:58.546Z", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "cli", "cwd": "/Users/divadbaroon/Desktop/engelbart-canvas", "sessionId": "a2f80be0-c548-4c0f-add0-bdf6bd4a276f", "version": "2.1.246", "gitBranch": "fix/canvas-zoom-cull"}
{"parentUuid": "1d89add3-a91f-4ce7-bd9b-70873a98c498", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5", "id": "msg_01VAYKVroEIAZv00KJe7RINQ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Fpqrd6XCzmr7Wt8EAuKShh", "name": "Edit", "input": {"file_path": "/Users/divadbaroon/Desktop/engelbart-canvas/src/renderer/canvas/culling.js", "old_string": "// Which cards to draw this frame.\nexport function visibleCards(cards, vp, margin = 120) {\n  const x0 = -vp.panX - margin;\n  const y0 = -vp.panY - margin;\n  const x1 = x0 + vp.width + 2 * margin;\n  const y1 = y0 + vp.height + 2 * margin;", "new_string": "import { toWorld } from './viewport.js';\n\n// Which cards to draw this frame. The viewport is in screen px; cards are in world units, so convert the\n// screen rectangle to world space first (it used to skip the zoom, culling cards when zoomed out).\nexport function visibleCards(cards, vp, margin = 120) {\n  const m = margin / vp.zoom;\n  const tl = toWorld(vp, 0, 0);\n  const br = toWorld(vp, vp.width, vp.height);\n  const x0 = tl.x - m, y0 = tl.y - m, x1 = br.x + m, y1 = br.y + m;"}}], "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2681, "cache_read_input_tokens": 33730, "output_tokens": 236, "service_tier": "standard"}}, "requestId": "req_011CMN32KMEQSt9fmcrdHUyR", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "14061cb5-3737-43d9-ba31-8c68dd749ab5", "timestamp": "2026-09-02T05:42:04.620Z", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "cli", "cwd": "/Users/divadbaroon/Desktop/engelbart-canvas", "sessionId": "a2f80be0-c548-4c0f-add0-bdf6bd4a276f", "version": "2.1.246", "gitBranch": "fix/canvas-zoom-cull"}
